IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er2-common`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulation 33: additional conditions and terms in relation to teachers.
-- Piece er2 (Sonnet 5.5), LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Every src:N is a line of SOR-96-332.txt, an unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- "Benefits payable under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act" are the benefits for pregnancy (s 22), for a new-born or adopted child
-- (s 23), for the care of a family member (s 23.1), of a critically ill child (s 23.2) and of a critically ill adult (s 23.3): the core's
-- `Reason for benefits` (paragraphs 12(3)(a), (b), (d), (e), (f)). Sickness benefits (s 21, paragraph 12(3)(c)) are NOT among them.

§ `Regulation 33(1) - definitions`

-- src:504 | 33 (1) The definitions in this subsection apply in this section.
-- src:505 | non-teaching period means the period that occurs annually at regular or irregular intervals during which no work is performed by a significant number of people employed in teaching. (période de congé)
-- src:506 | teaching means the occupation of teaching in a pre-elementary, an elementary or a secondary school, including a technical or vocational school. (enseignement)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 33(1) "teaching" (src:504) (src:506)
GIVEN `the occupation is the occupation of teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a pre-elementary school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in an elementary school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a secondary school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a technical or vocational school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 33(1) teaching` IF
        `the occupation is the occupation of teaching`
    AND (   `in a pre-elementary school`
         OR `in an elementary school`
         OR `in a secondary school`
         OR `in a technical or vocational school`)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 33(1) "non-teaching period" (src:504) (src:505)
GIVEN `the period occurs annually at regular or irregular intervals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no work is performed during it by a significant number of people employed in teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- "a significant number" is a judgment of whoever decides the claim; it is an input.
DECIDE `reg 33(1) non-teaching period` IF
        `the period occurs annually at regular or irregular intervals`
    AND `no work is performed during it by a significant number of people employed in teaching`

§ `Regulation 33(2) - no benefits in a non-teaching period`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 33(2) (src:507)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 33(2) the benefits are payable under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act` IF
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `pregnancy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `caring for a new-born or adopted child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `care or support of a family member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill adult` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:507 | (2) A claimant who was employed in teaching for any part of the claimant’s qualifying period is not entitled to receive benefits, other than those payable under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act, for any week of unemployment that falls in any non-teaching period of the claimant unless
-- src:508 | (a) the claimant's contract of employment for teaching has terminated;
-- src:509 | (b) the claimant's employment in teaching was on a casual or substitute basis; or
-- src:510 | (c) the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in respect of employment in an occupation other than teaching.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 33(2) (src:507-510)
GIVEN `the claimant was employed in teaching for any part of the claimant's qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week of unemployment falls in a non-teaching period of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the claimant's contract of employment for teaching has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's employment in teaching was on a casual or substitute basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in respect of employment in an occupation other than teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- The reason for the benefits is the claimant's own: "other than those payable under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3".
-- The three exceptions (a) to (c) are alternatives ("unless (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ...").
DECIDE `reg 33(2) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for the week of unemployment` IF
        `the claimant was employed in teaching for any part of the claimant's qualifying period`
    AND `the week of unemployment falls in a non-teaching period of the claimant`
    AND (NOT (`reg 33(2) the benefits are payable under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act` reason))
    AND (NOT (   `the claimant's contract of employment for teaching has terminated`
              OR `the claimant's employment in teaching was on a casual or substitute basis`
              OR `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in respect of employment in an occupation other than teaching`))

§ `Regulation 33(3) - the amount limited to the other occupation`

-- src:511 | (3) Where a claimant who was employed in teaching for any part of the claimant's qualifying period qualifies to receive benefits in respect of employment in an occupation other than teaching, the amount of benefits payable for a week of unemployment that falls within any non-teaching period of the claimant shall be limited to the amount that is payable in respect of the employment in that other occupation.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 33(3) (src:511)
GIVEN `the claimant was employed in teaching for any part of the claimant's qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in respect of employment in an occupation other than teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week of unemployment falls within a non-teaching period of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount that is payable in respect of the employment in that other occupation` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of benefits that would otherwise be payable for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "limited to": the benefits payable cannot exceed the amount payable in respect of the other occupation.
DECIDE `reg 33(3) the amount of benefits payable for the week of unemployment` IS
    IF       `the claimant was employed in teaching for any part of the claimant's qualifying period`
         AND `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in respect of employment in an occupation other than teaching`
         AND `the week of unemployment falls within a non-teaching period of the claimant`
    THEN min `the amount that is payable in respect of the employment in that other occupation` `the amount of benefits that would otherwise be payable for the week`
    ELSE `the amount of benefits that would otherwise be payable for the week`
